  "Number": 3,
  "Question": "Which of the following operations has the same effect on a number as multiplying by \\(\\dfrac34\\) and then dividing by \\(\\dfrac35?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "dividing by \\(\\dfrac43\\)",
    "B": "dividing by \\(\\dfrac{9}{20}\\)",
    "C": "multiplying by \\(\\dfrac{9}{20}\\)",
    "D": "dividing by \\(\\dfrac54\\)",
    "E": "multiplying by \\(\\dfrac54\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "E",
  "Solution": "Dividing by the nonzero fraction \\(3/5\\) means multiplying by its reciprocal, \\(5/3\\). Thus, for any starting number \\(x\\), the two operations give\n\\[\n\\left(x\\cdot\\frac34\\right)\\div\\frac35\n=x\\cdot\\frac34\\cdot\\frac53\n=x\\cdot\\frac54.\n\\]\nThe same effect is therefore multiplying by \\(\\boxed{\\frac54}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{E}\\).",
